Z||000000||Sootah||12-04-2001||10:19 AM||||Mkay now PFF members I need some advice; mkay?<BR>1<sup>st</sup> question: How easy is it to transfer a plate from one vehicle to another? Legally, mind you, I know you only have to pop the screws out.<P>2<sup>nd</sup>:Ya think that people would know what ANTIRIC means?<P>I'm actually wanting to get a plate that just says SOOTAH on it, but that would be for the Black Beauty. She's not running yet so I wondered if I could get the SOOTAH plate, stick it on my soon-to-be 86 SE, and when <B>BB</B> is fixed then have the plate transferred to her. This would be when the ANTIRIC plate would come into play. Or something similar. Any suggestions?<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__tig_sig2.gif">          <BR><sup><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Black_Beauty_-_Front_Right.jpg" TARGET=_blank>The Black Beauty</A> (85 GT) - <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Busted-Ass_SE.jpg" TARGET=_blank>Bustedato</A> (86 SE, Parts car)<BR><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I></sup> <BR><sup><B>AOL IM</B>: KSSouter<BR><B>MSN IM</B>: I_R_Sootah@hotmail.com<BR></sup>||||reg||1
Z||000001||JohnF||12-04-2001||10:33 AM||||Don't know the laws in your part of the woods but, here in the Lone Star State, plates (and any included numbers/letters) are assigned by VIN.<P>Can you get a transfer later?  Probably.  Just ask your friendly license-plate-passer-outer!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001112&p=56509969&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||9
Z||000002||Formula88||12-04-2001||12:15 PM||||In NC, it can be done.  Just tell the DMV what you want to do and pay the fee.<P>Let me guess, Anti-Rice?<P>I had WARPDRIV on my 72 Trans Am, and you wouldn't believe how many people DIDN'T get it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">||||reg||6
